==Enemy==
Like [[Tackey]] and [[Hackey]] before him, Ackey's attacks can easily snipe your important support units from afar. His health is actually among the lowest of his variants, but he has a [[Shield]] that can tank almost nine times as much and could regenerate once. The problems don't end here, as Ackey's attack is split into three rapid hits that get progressively weaker but can occasionally freeze your cats in place. Due to the multi-hit, he approximately has a 66% chance of freezing any cats he hits.

==Strategy==
Depending on the stage in which Ackey appears, it may be worth trying to get a powerful attacker in his range by having said attacker be approached by Ackey while the meatshield line is dangerously close to said attacker. This isn't easy to achieve given the frontline pressure, but it's always worth trying to exploit any openings. A much less risky way to deal with him is to use short-ranged cats, as anything with less than 350 range will easily reach his blind spot, if they can get past the attack. Short-ranged [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercers]] such as a level 32 [[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]] can instantly kill an unbuffed Ackey and easily rush into his blind spot.

