==Trivia==
*Ackey's projectile is a dodecahedron.
*Ackey's name may be a pun on [[wikipedia:ja:悪鬼|悪鬼 ''akki'']] (one of several Japanese words that can be translated as "demon" or "evil spirit"; the individual kanji mean "evil" and "''[[wikipedia:Oni|oni]]''") and ''[[Tackey]]''. Other than especially sinister ''oni'', the word 悪鬼 ''akki'' can be used figuratively to mean someone who commits acts of extreme evil.
*Ackey's Japanese name, Devil Katsuya, is seemingly a mash-up of '''Ka'''zuya and Ta'''tsuya''', twin brothers of the baseball manga ''[[wikipedia:Touch (manga)|Touch]]'', which is also referenced by Tackey's Japanese name and description.
**Just like Tackey's Japanese description, Ackey's mirrors the character of Tatsuya, a  high-school baseball player who rose to glory to continue his deceased brother's legacy. But where Tatsuya's brother died in a traffic accident, Ackey's twin's death was purely his own doing.
**Devil Katsuya may also be a reference to ''Tekken'' antagonist [[wikia:Tekken:Devil Kazuya|Devil Kazuya]].
*In baseball, a five-tool player is someone who hits for average and for power, runs the bases well, fields well and throws well.
*Contrary to Ackey's Japanese description, the third role entailed by a "[https://jisho.org/word/三刀流 three sword style]" (三刀流 ''santōryū'') in Japanese baseball terminology is normally fielder, not manager.
*Prior to [[Version 14.2 Update|Version 14.2]], Ackey's second and third hits landed at frames 38 and 44 respectively. They were changed to properly fit his attack animation, as before all three hits were grouped within only the first blast.

